<body>

<!-- COVER -->
<div class="cover">
  <div class="cover-tag">Energy Markets &middot; Trend Analysis</div>
  <h1>Global Crude Oil Price Trends:<br>A Historical Analysis (1970–2026)</h1>
  <div class="cover-sub">A comprehensive examination of monthly crude oil prices spanning 56 years — from the pre-embargo era through the energy transition. Covering 675 monthly observations, key price regimes, major shocks, and structural market shifts.</div>
  <div class="cover-meta">
    <div>Dataset: <span>Jan 1970 – Mar 2026</span></div>
    <div>Observations: <span>675 Monthly Data Points</span></div>
    <div>Prepared: <span>April 2026</span></div>
    <div>Audience: <span>Energy Market Analysts</span></div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="container">

<!-- TOC -->
<div class="toc">
  <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#executive-overview">Executive Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#long-term-trend">Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</a></li>
    <li><a href="#decade-by-decade">Decade-by-Decade Breakdown</a></li>
    <li><a href="#volatility-and-shocks">Price Volatility &amp; Major Shocks</a></li>
    <li><a href="#statistical-summary">Statistical Summary &amp; Distribution</a></li>
    <li><a href="#outlook-and-conclusions">Outlook &amp; Conclusions</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE OVERVIEW ===== -->
<div class="section" id="executive-overview">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">1</div>
    <h2>Executive Overview</h2>
  </div>

  <p>This report analyzes 675 monthly crude oil price observations spanning January 1970 through March 2026, sourced from a global benchmark dataset. Prices are denominated in nominal US dollars per barrel (USD/bbl) and are not inflation-adjusted — all comparisons are in nominal terms unless stated otherwise.</p>

  <p>Over the 56-year period, crude oil prices rose from <strong>$1.21/bbl</strong> in January 1970 to <strong>$87.84/bbl</strong> in March 2026, implying a compound annual growth rate (CAGR) of <strong>7.93%</strong>. However, this trajectory was far from linear: prices were shaped by five decades of geopolitical shocks, supply cartels, financial crises, a global pandemic, and the emergence of US shale production. The all-time high of <strong>$132.83/bbl</strong> was recorded in July 2008, while the all-time low of <strong>$1.21/bbl</strong> persisted across all of 1970 — a nominal price range of <strong>$131.62/bbl</strong>.</p>

  <!-- KPI Grid -->
  <div class="kpi-grid">
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Price Range</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$131.62</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">$1.21 min &rarr; $132.83 max</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">CAGR (1970–2026)</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">7.93%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Nominal USD, annualized</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Std Deviation</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">$30.59</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Full-period price dispersion</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Max MoM Change</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">+217%</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Jan 1974 (Oil Embargo shock)</div>
    </div>
    <div class="kpi-card">
      <div class="kpi-label">Highest-Avg Decade</div>
      <div class="kpi-value">2010s</div>
      <div class="kpi-sub">Average $76.45/bbl</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="callout">
    <strong>Key Finding:</strong> The 2000s and 2010s together represent a structural step-change in the price level — driven by China-led demand growth, peak-oil anxiety, OPEC discipline, and geopolitical conflict — elevating average prices from the $18.19/bbl of the 1990s to the $76.45/bbl average of the 2010s. The 2020s (so far) average $71.75/bbl, shaped by pandemic collapse and subsequent post-Ukraine war energy crisis.
  </div>

  <p>The distribution of prices is <strong>right-skewed</strong>: the median price ($29.11/bbl) is substantially below the mean ($39.80/bbl), reflecting that the majority of monthly observations occurred during low-price regimes, while episodic spikes pull the average upward. Over half of all monthly readings have been below $30/bbl.</p>
</div>

<!-- ===== SECTION 2: LONG-TERM TREND ===== -->
<div class="section" id="long-term-trend">
  <div class="section-header">
    <div class="section-num">2</div>
    <h2>Long-Term Price Trajectory (1970–2026)</h2>
  </div>

  <p>The full monthly time series reveals four structurally distinct price regimes: a low-price pre-embargo era (1970–1972), an OPEC-dominated plateau (1974–1985), a prolonged era of moderate prices (1986–2002), and a high-volatility elevated-price era (2003–2026). No single decade resembles another — each carries its own defining price logic.</p>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <div class="chart-title">Monthly Crude Oil Price — Full Time Series (Jan 1970 – Mar 2026)</div>
    <div class="chart-sub">USD per barrel (nominal). Annotations mark major structural inflection points.</div>
    <canvas id="mainChart" style="height:400px;"></canvas>
  </div>

  <div class="chart-box">
    <div class="chart-title">Annual Average Crude Oil Price (1970–2026)</div>
    <div class="chart-sub">Simple average of monthly prices within each calendar year.</div>
    <canvas id="annualChart" style="height:300px;"></canvas>
  </div>

  <h3>Phase Analysis</h3>
  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Phase</th>
          <th>Period</th>
          <th class="num">Avg Price</th>
          <th class="num">Peak</th>
          <th class="num">Trough</th>
          <th>Defining Dynamic</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Pre-Embargo</strong></td>
          <td>1970–1973</td>
          <td class="num">$1.86</td>
          <td class="num">$4.10</td>
          <td class="num">$1.21</td>
          <td>Fixed administered pricing; marginal increments</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>OPEC Shock I &amp; II</strong></td>
          <td>1974–1981</td>
          <td class="num">$22.10</td>
          <td class="num">$40.75</td>
          <td class="num">$10.00</td>
          <td>Arab Oil Embargo (1973) &amp; Iranian Revolution (1979)</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>Price Collapse &amp; Stabilization</strong></td>
          <td>1982–1999</td>
